  "scope": "native lethal death at Lumbridge, respawn, floor-item Take of death drops with full-inventory refusal, native Drop, retry Take exactly once, then native file save and fresh-player restore",
  "test": {
    "file": "upstream/game-server/game/src/test/kotlin/content/area/misthalin/lumbridge/church/DeathLootRecoveryTest.kt",
    "sha256": "19aa3f8e977ba7f5198f4c170f2afe1e7d15414df36632e334872a094850a602",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "Full inventory Take refuses the death drop then succeeds exactly once after a native Drop",
        "death": "player.damage(101) at Tile(3235, 3220), same API as GravestonesTest; respawn at Tile(3221, 3219)",
        "fixture": "supplied logs, bronze_dagger, bronze_sword, tinderbox; raw_shrimps x25 filler added after respawn",
        "derived_drop": "tinderbox (lowest cache cost among supplied); logs, bronze_dagger, bronze_sword kept",
        "walk_arrival": "asserted: player.tile == Tile(3234, 3220), distance 1 from the grave tile, not the grave tile, after each walk",
        "save_restore": {
          "method": "SaveQueue(FileStorage(dir)).direct().join() into an isolated Files.createTempDirectory owned by the test, PlayerSave.load, Despawn.player + Players.remove, save.toPlayer(), AccountManager setup/index/spawn, tick(3); dir deleted in finally",
          "expected_snapshot": "tile, experience and every inventory copied from the live player before the save, not aliased to the save",
          "asserted": [
            "restored tile equals the saved tile",
            "experience array equals the live array",
            "every inventory instance id set and item array equals the live array",
            "recovered item count is exactly 1 in the fresh player",
            "kept originals (logs, bronze_dagger, bronze_sword) each count 1 in the fresh player",
            "creation marker survives restore"
          ]
        },
        "result": "PASSED"
      }
    ],
    "limits": [
      "Death uses the damage API, not a real combat encounter.",
      "The supplied inventory is an explicit fixture; no earned progression.",
      "The refused Take's ordinary approach stepped the player onto the grave tile; the test walks back to Tile(3234, 3220) before the native Drop, which is refused on the grave tile.",
      "No teleport is used; the walks use the Walk instruction helper.",
      "The save restore runs in-process against a temp save directory; it is not a login through a live session, owner save, or server process."
    ]
  },
  "corrections": [
    "The earlier claim that no test-visible helper applies a PlayerSave to a fresh Player was wrong. FullAdventureJourneyTest.verifyFreshPlayerRestore (lines 272-298) already uses save.toPlayer() with AccountManager setup/index/spawn, and this test now follows that pattern."
  ],
